{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1247434-a-question-of-a-notary-and-tokens","id":1247434,"title":"A question of a Notary and Tokens","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-18T11:05:30-07:00","id":1247434,"title":"A question of a Notary and Tokens","content":"This is a bit of a white-room scenario, but say that the pledge that a Notary has involves Tokens that explicitely designate them as belonging \u201cthe bearer of the contract, [Gentry name here]\u201d. Under normal circumstances, a Changeling using a Token that belongs to the Gentry would make them a Stolen token. However, could the Notary use these Tokens without such an issue? After all, since they bear the contract on their skin/blood/bones/soul, they are technically one of the parties the Tokens belong to (and could even be how they escaped Arcadia).<br /> <br /> I ask this to help revise the backstory for a character I\u2019ve got whose backstory is basically as a Doctor Who companion, and I can\u2019t decide between Playmate or Notary. I tried one game as a Playmate, but my ability to work as an effective social character was...not encouraging, let\u2019s just say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T17:29:55-07:00","id":1247560,"title":"","content":"This seems like the very definition of a situation where you ought to do what works best for your table, because this is a wholly homemade problem you're wrestling with.<br /> <br /> Are you planning on leaning into the metaphysical confusion between the Notary and their Keeper in any other ways?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T18:28:00-07:00","id":1247574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1247434-a-question-of-a-notary-and-tokens?p=1247560#post1247560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems like the very definition of a situation where you ought to do what works best for your table, because this is a wholly homemade problem you're wrestling with.<br /> <br /> Are you planning on leaning into the metaphysical confusion between the Notary and their Keeper in any other ways?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn\u2019t planning on evoking it in any significant manner. The confusion in the pledge was more an invention on why my character would a) be able to use a Token without his Keeper actively hunting him down for it (beyond normal anyways) b) why he would be both aware of the Token and where it was kept to escape with it. The Token to me would be the Nostalgia Cabinet, a wardrobe that, upon entering, can take the user to a place they\u2019ve already been to that they can remember...with the drawback that it doesn\u2019t cross realms without causing harm to the user, hence the Changeling who tried to escape with it being ejected into the Hedge rather than returning to Ironside. Outside of maybe using Faerie Favor to accellerate the re-acquisition of the Token, I\u2019m not sure what other scenarios confusing the Notary with their Gentry for the continued acquisition of Tokens may result with...although, it could start making the other Gentry in the contract getting involved, or justify Gentrified Bearing.<br /> <br /> The question on whether said confusion excludes him from the normal problems with a Stolen Token in that particular circumstance is one that I thought of later. If it simply allows the Changeling to claim \u201cthis Token no longer belongs to the bearer of the contract\u201d and thus divulge it from their Keeper\u2019s own holding (and thus revoke its status as a Stolen Token), rather than grants the Changeling unique access to the Token without drawing attention to themselves from their Gentry, then that works for me. Then again, that kind of process sounds anything but \u201csimple\u201d...<br /> <br /> Maybe I\u2019m looking too deeply into this kind of origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 08-18-2018, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T20:51:30-07:00","id":1247603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1247434-a-question-of-a-notary-and-tokens?p=1247574#post1247574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I\u2019m looking too deeply into this kind of origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>To cut a long statement short: You super are. &quot;You can have a token with any of the three origins and not give it the attached mechanical wrinkles&quot; is in the text.<br /> <br /> Unless you're aiming to specifically have the Cabinet suffer the mechanical effects of being a stolen token <i>and</i> it is imperative that your character and only your character be able to use it without the onset of paranoia or putting out a call to very real fae threats, you can just say that you stole it and have that not come with mechanical consequences.<br /> <br /> Like, do you <i>want</i> to use the TARDIS more than once a week without living like more of a fugitive than is normal for the Lost? Because there's a case to be made that what happened here is less that you stole a token and more that you found your Keeper's Steed and made a deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T23:53:05-07:00","id":1247625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1247434-a-question-of-a-notary-and-tokens?p=1247603#post1247603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To cut a long statement short: You super are. &quot;You can have a token with any of the three origins and not give it the attached mechanical wrinkles&quot; is in the text.<br /> <br /> Unless you're aiming to specifically have the Cabinet suffer the mechanical effects of being a stolen token <i>and</i> it is imperative that your character and only your character be able to use it without the onset of paranoia or putting out a call to very real fae threats, you can just say that you stole it and have that not come with mechanical consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have an exceptional ability to cut to a salubrious solution Satchel. Too often I get wrapped up in ideas to simply stop and look at the material I'm getting the ideas from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, do you <i>want</i> to use the TARDIS more than once a week without living like more of a fugitive than is normal for the Lost? Because there's a case to be made that what happened here is less that you stole a token and more that you found your Keeper's Steed and made a deal with it. </div> </div> </div>Well, less a Steed and more &quot;object that I don't want to use because part of my Title requires that I can't do the same thing twice, and going to a place I've already been to leads to that&quot;...but now I'm remembering about the Empty Room from Mysterious Places...maybe there is a case for a steed after all. There are even Dread Powers that can serve it admirably...however, that's perhaps better for a written story (or to run as a storyteller) than to ask of a storyteller as a player.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback Satchel. Really helped unclutter the idea, and give me some more practical ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":".  Corrected terms for the proper tone 08-19-2018, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}